Peter Brown here with another GameSpot  news update the NPD numbers are out for  June and what do you know the Xbox one  sold twice as many systems as it did in  May but despite that the PlayStation 4  was still the best-selling console the  NPD group has released their monthly  sales figures and the respective console  manufacturers have released statements  based on the report microsoft announced  that Xbox one sales had more than  doubled from May to June after its  connect list four hundred dollar model  went on sale later sony said in a  statement that the playstation 4 came  out on top in the US during june noting  that this is the sixth month in a row  that the playstation 4 has been the top  seller sony also said that the  playstation 4 was a top platform for  physical software sales among the new  generation of consoles sales of the Wii  U continue to rise thanks to the launch  of Mario Kart 8 compared to June of 2013  wii u sales are up two hundred and  thirty-three percent 3ds sales are up  fifty-five percent over May but the NPD  group noted that there was a  year-over-year decline in portable  hardware sales compared to June of last  year though hardware sales are up 106  percent bringing in 290 2.7 million  dollars this year compared to 142  million dollars this time last year as  far as software goes wash dogs is the  overall highest seller win counting all  five of its platforms while Mario Kart 8  was the number one when comparing  individual products brawl your video  game and number related news stay tuned  to gamespot com
 

